      "text": "France's eastern border with Germany was sealed by the Maginot Line. That left the Low Countries — the open plain of central Belgium, the 1914 invasion route — and, between them, the Ardennes: forested hills and gorges that French planners judged too slow for a modern army.\n\nThe Allied plan was to rush into Belgium and meet the Germans on the Dyle line.",
